/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  ctrl21_tank_level_control -- the most common loop of a plant: INVENTORY.

  The same water tank as unsteady05 (D = 2 m, area 3.1416 m2), but its outflow
  is a MANIPULATED FLOW (a flow-controlled pump: `mode flow`, mv F_out), so
  the level INTEGRATES the difference of the flows,

      A rho/MW dh/dt = F_in - F_out          plant gain a = MW/(rho A)
                                              = 5.7e-3 m/s per kmol/s (rho = 1001.55 kg/m3)

  and nothing brings it back: an integrating process.  A level controller
  closes the loop on F_out.  The inflow steps at t = 600 s from 0.20 to
  0.30 kmol/s (a Signal on the tank's inlet face).

  THE SIGN.  The controller is direct-acting on error = setpoint - level, and
  a level ABOVE the setpoint must RAISE the outflow, so the gains are
  NEGATIVE (u = bias + Kp (SP - h) + Ki Int(SP - h) with Kp < 0).  Bias
  0.20 kmol/s is the outflow that balances the old inflow.

  WHAT THE TWO CONTROLLERS DO (measured; check_dynamic_tank re-runs both):

    PI  (Kp = -2, Ki = -0.01):  the integral term removes the offset; the
        level returns to the 2.0 m setpoint (zero offset), after a peak
        excursion of 0.031 m (max |h - 2| in trajectory.csv; the end offset is
        < 1e-7 m).
    P-only (Ki = 0, edit one line):  the outflow must rise by 0.10 kmol/s
        and a proportional-only controller can only do that with an error,
          F_out = bias + Kp (SP - h)  ->  h - SP = (F_in,new - bias)/|Kp|
                = 0.10 / 2 = 0.050 m   (offset: the level settles at 2.05 m).

  The closed loop is second order, wn^2 = a |Ki| , 2 zeta wn = a |Kp|:
  wn = 7.6e-3 1/s, zeta = 0.76.  The inflow is a disturbance the loop must
  reject; the tank's own buffering (volume) is what the controller trades
  against the downstream flow's smoothness -- loose level control is a
  feature, not a defect, when the outflow feeds another unit.

  ENERGY.  H on the elements datum, T a readout; the ledger claims mass and
  energy and closes (check_dynamic_tank).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        tank;
        type        dynamicTank;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( product );

        operation
        {
            geometry
            {
                shape       verticalCylinder;
                diameter    2.0 m;
                height      4.0 m;
            }

            outflow
            {
                mode        flow;
                F           0.20 kmol/s;     // initial; the controller takes over
            }
        }
    }
);

controllers
(
    {
        name         FeedStep;
        type         Signal;

        actuator     { unit tank;  inletField F; }

        signal
        {
            type        step;
            mean        0.20;              // kmol/s of water
            step        0.10;              // +50 % at tStep
            tStep       600.0;             // s
        }
    }

    {
        name         LC1;
        type         PID;

        measurement  { unit tank;  cv level; }
        actuator     { unit tank;  mv F_out; }

        setpoint     2.0;                  // m

        gains
        {
            Kp       -2.0;                 // kmol/s per m  (negative: reverse acting)
            Ki       -0.01;                // kmol/s per (m s)
            Kd       0.0;
        }

        output
        {
            min      0.0;
            max      1.0;
            bias     0.20;                 // the outflow that balances the old inflow
        }
    }
);
